d the difference  is shocking you might think that 6.1  inches isn't that much smaller than 6.7  but when you start using these the 12  pro max really stands out  every time i pull this phone out and i  look at the display i start using it  i'm just surprised by how large it is  and how nice it is um now  as far as productivity and with that i  mean email  web browsing there's really not that  much of a difference other than just  everything being  bigger you don't really benefit that  much from that screen size  where it really starts to come in is if  you're watching  videos now it's not a massive difference  but you definitely  notice it especially if you're actually  switching over to say like a movie  and with that one difference that i  thought there could be  is speakers i thought the larger phone  could have better sound but in reality i  didn't notice any difference both sound  just as loud  the quality sounds just as good but the  real big difference  as far as the displays is gaming  i was playing some games mostly call of  duty mobile on the 12  pro and i kept having that thought of  man i wish  the screen was bigger all the icons are  small i'm not seeing as much as far as  far away enemies  it's just so limiting and the experience  wasn't great now when i got the 12 pro  max in oh my goodness the difference in  gaming is dramatic so i would say if  you're somebody that plays games  often especially competitive games it is  awesome having that larger display  and now let's talk about the biggest  reason why some people want to move up  in size  to the max model when they've always had  a smaller iphone  and that is camera quality the pro max  not only has a 2.5 times telephoto lens  instead of a two times telephoto lens  but  the main sensor it actually has sensor  stabilization now  and with that a much larger sensor size  as well  that means it should help out in low  light photos and everything should be  smoother  honestly i didn't see that much of 